# Shared SARA definitions

Use this unannotated module only for facts, types, and provision-neutral helper
computations shared by multiple statutory sections. Do not place a statutory
rule, required evaluator output, or cross-section API orchestration here.

SARA factual-input and ground-truth conventions:

- A residence fact links a resident in `subject_1` (an internal event agent) to
  a home/place entity in `relative_1` (an internal event patient). Its
  `identifier` identifies the residence event, not the home. Two people can
  have separate residence events whose patients identify the same home;
  co-residence does not require both people to be agents of one event.
  A household-maintenance payment can reference that home/place entity in
  `purpose_1` or `purpose_2`, rather than referencing a residence event.
- `gross_income_individual` returns only the named person's income and
  received payments. It does not combine joint filers' incomes. A joint-return
  event identifies its filers through its subjects/agents;
  `has_full_year_joint_return` checks that relationship and its year boundaries,
  without aggregating any money. The SARA ground-truth computation combines
  the two spouses' individual incomes when they have an applicable full-year
  joint return; using the individual helper alone does not reproduce that
  combined tax base.
- An omitted service location is represented by absent location slots and an
  empty internal `locations` list. The original SARA benchmark treats a service
  with no location fact as performed in the United States (see
  `data/prolog/sara/statutes/section3306.pl`, `s3306_c_A`). This is a benchmark
  convention for absent factual input, not a claim that the statute supplies a
  general location default. The fixed input helpers preserve the absence;
  they do not insert `UnitedStates`. Explicitly supplied locations remain
  supplied locations and must not be treated as absent merely because they
  are represented by a named place instead of the `UnitedStates` literal.


- Missing payment means remains absent in the internal event view. For the
  agricultural cash-remuneration threshold specifically, the original SARA
  ground truth accepts either no recorded means or an explicitly cash payment
  (`section3306.pl`, `s3306_c_1_A_i`). Do not require a `Cash` value for that
  threshold when means is absent, and do not generalize this convention to
  every statutory test involving a payment medium.
- `multiplicity` can encode repeated grounded solutions or a group of distinct,
  interchangeable workers compressed into one representative service/payment
  pair. For a compressed worker group, the monetary amount is per represented
  worker and multiplicity is the number of represented workers. For example,
  six workers paid $5,012 each can appear as amount $5,012 with multiplicity 6.
  A per-worker wage cap applies before scaling by group size:
  `min(5012, 7000) * 6`, not `min(5012 * 6, 7000)`. Matching service and payment
  rows can both carry that same group multiplicity; multiplying those counts
  together would count the group twice. `weighted_amounts` scales raw amounts
  only; it does not apply per-worker caps or compute headcounts.
- An `ItemizeDeductions` event can record an explicit election, but the protected
  SARA inputs do not always include such an event when the case narrative
  elects itemization. The original ground truth selects the itemized path when
  `s63_d` finds at least one dated deduction fact for the taxpayer in the tax
  year; the standard-deduction path requires that no such facts exist
  (`section63.pl`, `s63_b` and `s63_d`). A separate election event, or a strictly
  positive deduction total, is not required by that benchmark selection test.
  The fixed input helpers do not synthesize an election event.

Canonical input views: `parent_links` orients parent-child aliases;
`sibling_links` merges symmetric aliases; `date_of_birth` prefers an explicit
Birth fact and accepts relationship dates only when its fallback flag is true.
Birth dates and relationship-effective dates can legitimately differ (adoption).
Repeated event identities are deduplicated in event views, while gross income
counts consistent Income/Payment aliases once per transaction identity. Equal
amounts on different transaction identities remain distinct. Callers must use
input consistency validation before evaluation: gold `Api.TotalTaxFromWorld`
validates through `ValidatedWorld`; the raw API carries equivalent assertions.
The public World uses five lists. Legacy numbered slots are accepted only by
the Python migration adapter, which removes unused entries before conversion.

> Module Definitions

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration TermKind: # Distinguishes Prolog atoms from Prolog strings with the same encoded identity.
  -- Atom # Entity originated as a Prolog atom.
  -- String # Entity originated as a Prolog string.

declaration structure Entity: # Identity of a Prolog atom or string, including people, organizations, and events.
  data id content integer # Encoded Prolog term identity; 0 is the absent-entity sentinel.
  data kind content TermKind # Original Prolog term category from TermKind.

declaration enumeration KnownValue: # Recognized literal values used in Prolog event attributes.
  -- AgriculturalLabor # Agricultural labor service classification.
  -- DomesticService # Domestic service classification.
  -- Cash # Cash as the means of payment.
  -- UnitedStates # United States location or country literal (usa).
  -- PrivateHome # Private-home service location.
  -- LocalCollegeClub # Local college club service location.
  -- CollegeFraternityOrSorority # College fraternity or sorority service location.
  -- SicknessProvision # Provision for sickness under a payment plan.
  -- AccidentDisabilityProvision # Provision for accident disability under a payment plan.
  -- DeathProvision # Provision for death under a payment plan.
  -- EmployeeOrDependentProvision # Plan provision for employees or their dependents.
  -- ReligiousOrganization # Religious organization classification.
  -- Government # Government classification.
  -- Hospital # Hospital classification.
  -- EducationalInstitution # Educational institution classification.
  -- Student # Student classification.
  -- ForeignGovernment # Foreign government classification.
  -- StateGovernment # State government classification.
  -- OtherKnownValue # Sentinel for no usable literal attribute; Known containing this value is removed from the event view.

declaration enumeration FactValue: # Literal or entity-valued attribute; absence uses Known OtherKnownValue or Named with Entity.id = 0, rather than an optional type.
  -- Known content KnownValue # Recognized literal attribute, carried as a KnownValue.
  -- Named content Entity # Named attribute, carried as an Entity reference.

declaration enumeration EventKind: # Prolog event predicates and entity classifications in the common event view.
  -- Marriage # Marriage event.
  -- Birth # Birth event; its start records the birth date.
  -- Death # Death event.
  -- Income # Income event; the agent is the income recipient.
  -- Payment # Payment event; the agent pays and the patient receives.
  -- Service # Service event; the agent works for the patient employer.
  -- Residence # Residence event; subjects/agents are residents, relatives/patients identify the home/place, and identifier identifies the event rather than the home.
  -- Migration # Migration event.
  -- Retirement # Retirement event.
  -- Deduction # Deduction fact; dated taxpayer deduction facts can select the SARA GT itemized path without an ItemizeDeductions event.
  -- Enrollment # Enrollment event.
  -- Termination # Termination event.
  -- Incarceration # Incarceration event.
  -- LegalSeparation # Legal-separation event.
  -- JointReturn # Joint tax return whose agents are the joint filers.
  -- ItemizeDeductions # Explicit election to itemize deductions when supplied; SARA GT may instead select itemization from dated deduction facts without this event.
  -- Blindness # Blindness status.
  -- Disability # Disability status.
  -- AttendingClasses # Class-attendance status.
  -- MedicalPatient # Medical-patient status.
  -- NonresidentAlien # Recorded nonresident-alien status; retained in the internal event list. NoStatusFact is the legacy no-fact marker; native status inputs use an empty list when absent.
  -- Citizenship # Citizenship fact.
  -- Son # Son relationship; agent is the son and patient is the parent.
  -- Daughter # Daughter relationship; agent is the daughter and patient is the parent.
  -- Father # Father relationship; agent is the father and patient is the child.
  -- Mother # Mother relationship; agent is the mother and patient is the child.
  -- Brother # Brother relationship; agent is the brother of the patient.
  -- Sister # Sister relationship; agent is the sister of the patient.
  -- Sibling # Sibling relationship between agent and patient.
  -- Business # Entity classified as a business.
  -- BusinessTrust # Entity classified as a business trust.
  -- Plan # Entity classified as a payment or benefit plan.
  -- Hospital # Hospital classification.
  -- MedicalInstitution # Entity classified as a medical institution.
  -- PenalInstitution # Entity classified as a penal institution.
  -- EducationalInstitution # Educational institution classification.
  -- NursesTrainingSchool # Entity classified as a nurses training school.
  -- InternationalOrganization # Entity classified as an international organization.
  -- AmericanEmployer # Entity classified as an American employer.
  -- UnemploymentCompensationAgreement # Unemployment-compensation agreement fact.

declaration enumeration FinancialFactKind: # Kinds of external financial facts, including a legacy no-fact marker.
  -- NoFinancialFact # Legacy no-fact marker; omitted from the internal event list. Use an empty list for absent native inputs.
  -- Income # Income event; the agent is the income recipient.
  -- Payment # Payment event; the agent pays and the patient receives.
  -- Deduction # Deduction fact; dated taxpayer deduction facts can select the SARA GT itemized path without an ItemizeDeductions event.

declaration enumeration RelationshipFactKind: # Kinds of external relationship facts, including a legacy no-fact marker.
  -- NoRelationshipFact # Legacy no-fact marker; omitted from the internal event list. Use an empty list for absent native inputs.
  -- Marriage # Marriage event.
  -- Birth # Birth event; its start records the birth date.
  -- Death # Death event.
  -- Residence # Residence event; subjects/agents are residents, relatives/patients identify the home/place, and identifier identifies the event rather than the home.
  -- Migration # Migration event.
  -- LegalSeparation # Legal-separation event.
  -- JointReturn # Joint tax return whose agents are the joint filers.
  -- Son # Son relationship; agent is the son and patient is the parent.
  -- Daughter # Daughter relationship; agent is the daughter and patient is the parent.
  -- Father # Father relationship; agent is the father and patient is the child.
  -- Mother # Mother relationship; agent is the mother and patient is the child.
  -- Brother # Brother relationship; agent is the brother of the patient.
  -- Sister # Sister relationship; agent is the sister of the patient.
  -- Sibling # Sibling relationship between agent and patient.

declaration enumeration EmploymentFactKind: # Kinds of external employment and institution facts, including a legacy no-fact marker.
  -- NoEmploymentFact # Legacy no-fact marker; omitted from the internal event list. Use an empty list for absent native inputs.
  -- Service # Service event; the agent works for the patient employer.
  -- Retirement # Retirement event.
  -- Business # Entity classified as a business.
  -- BusinessTrust # Entity classified as a business trust.
  -- Plan # Entity classified as a payment or benefit plan.
  -- Hospital # Hospital classification.
  -- MedicalInstitution # Entity classified as a medical institution.
  -- PenalInstitution # Entity classified as a penal institution.
  -- EducationalInstitution # Educational institution classification.
  -- NursesTrainingSchool # Entity classified as a nurses training school.
  -- InternationalOrganization # Entity classified as an international organization.
  -- AmericanEmployer # Entity classified as an American employer.

declaration enumeration StatusFactKind: # Kinds of external status facts, including a legacy no-fact marker.
  -- NoStatusFact # Legacy no-fact marker; omitted from the internal event list. Use an empty list for absent native inputs.
  -- Enrollment # Enrollment event.
  -- Termination # Termination event.
  -- Incarceration # Incarceration event.
  -- ItemizeDeductions # Explicit election to itemize deductions when supplied; SARA GT may instead select itemization from dated deduction facts without this event.
  -- Blindness # Blindness status.
  -- Disability # Disability status.
  -- AttendingClasses # Class-attendance status.
  -- MedicalPatient # Medical-patient status.
  -- NonresidentAlien # Recorded nonresident-alien status; retained in the internal event list. NoStatusFact is the legacy no-fact marker; native status inputs use an empty list when absent.
  -- Citizenship # Citizenship fact.
  -- UnemploymentCompensationAgreement # Unemployment-compensation agreement fact.

declaration structure Event: # Internal common view of a Prolog event or classified entity and its associated facts.
  data identifier content Entity # Entity identifying this event or classified organization, institution, or plan.
  data kind content EventKind # Fact classification selected from EventKind.
  data agents content list of Entity # People or organizations acting in the event or holding the status, such as workers, joint filers, or residents; separate residents may have separate events at the same home.
  data patients content list of Entity # People or entities receiving or affected by the action, such as employers or payment recipients; for Residence, these are home/place entities, not residence-event identifiers.
  data starts content list of date # Recorded start dates; an empty list means no recorded start.
  data ends content list of date # Recorded end dates; an empty list means no recorded end.
  data amounts content list of money # Monetary amounts before weighting by multiplicity.
  data purposes content list of FactValue # Work performed, benefits promised by a plan, or events that a payment compensates for, according to kind.
  data locations content list of FactValue # Places or institutions where the activity occurs.
  data means content list of FactValue # How payment is made: cash or a reference to the benefit plan providing it. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data reasons content list of FactValue # Causes of the event, such as disability or death leading to termination.
  data beneficiaries content list of Entity # People receiving benefits from the event or plan.
  data countries content list of FactValue # Countries associated with the event or geographical entity.
  data types content list of FactValue # Classifications of the activity or entity, such as agricultural labor or a business category.
  data destinations content list of FactValue # Places to which a person migrates.
  ## Number of represented grounded solutions or interchangeable workers; compressed worker groups require per-worker caps before scaling and must not be counted twice through matching service/payment rows.
  data multiplicity content integer # Number of represented grounded solutions or interchangeable workers; compressed worker groups require per-worker caps before scaling and must not be counted twice through matching service/payment rows.

## External facts are separated by legal-domain shape. `Event` remains an
## internal common view used by provisions that quantify across fact families.
declaration structure FinancialFact: # External income, payment, or deduction fact.
  data identifier content Entity # Entity identifying this event or classified organization, institution, or plan.
  data kind content FinancialFactKind # Fact classification selected from FinancialFactKind.
  data agent content Entity # Income recipient, payer, or person claiming a deduction, according to kind; id 0 means absent.
  data patient content Entity # Payment recipient or other entity affected by the financial fact; id 0 means absent.
  data start content date # Start date; used only when start_present is true.
  data end content date # End date; used only when end_present is true.
  data start_present content boolean # True when a start date is recorded; false makes start irrelevant.
  data end_present content boolean # True when an end date is recorded; false makes end irrelevant.
  data amount content money # Monetary amount before multiplicity scaling; for a compressed worker group this is per worker, so apply any per-worker cap before scaling.
  data purpose_1 content FactValue # What the payment compensates for, usually a Named reference to a service or termination event; household-maintenance payments may instead name the home/place entity linked by a Residence fact; entry 1. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data purpose_2 content FactValue # What the payment compensates for, usually a Named reference to a service or termination event; household-maintenance payments may instead name the home/place entity linked by a Residence fact; entry 2. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data means content FactValue # How payment is made: cash or a reference to the benefit plan providing it. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data beneficiary content Entity # Person receiving the benefit of a payment or plan; id 0 means absent.
  data multiplicity content integer # Number of represented grounded solutions or interchangeable workers; compressed worker groups require per-worker caps before scaling and must not be counted twice through matching service/payment rows.

declaration structure RelationshipFact: # External family, life-event, residence, or joint-return fact.
  data identifier content Entity # Entity identifying this event or classified organization, institution, or plan.
  data kind content RelationshipFactKind # Fact classification selected from RelationshipFactKind.
  data subject_1 content Entity # Person participating in the event, such as a spouse, joint filer, or the family member described by kind; entry 1; id 0 means absent.
  data subject_2 content Entity # Person participating in the event, such as a spouse, joint filer, or the family member described by kind; entry 2; id 0 means absent.
  data subject_3 content Entity # Person participating in the event, such as a spouse, joint filer, or the family member described by kind; entry 3; id 0 means absent.
  data subject_4 content Entity # Person participating in the event, such as a spouse, joint filer, or the family member described by kind; entry 4; id 0 means absent.
  data relative_1 content Entity # Entity related to the subject: e.g. the parent of a Son, child of a Father, or home/place occupied by a Residence subject; entry 1; id 0 means absent.
  data relative_2 content Entity # Entity related to the subject, interpreted by kind as for relative_1; entry 2; id 0 means absent.
  data start content date # Start date; used only when start_present is true.
  data end content date # End date; used only when end_present is true.
  data start_present content boolean # True when a start date is recorded; false makes start irrelevant.
  data end_present content boolean # True when an end date is recorded; false makes end irrelevant.
  data multiplicity content integer # Number of represented grounded solutions or interchangeable workers; compressed worker groups require per-worker caps before scaling and must not be counted twice through matching service/payment rows.

declaration structure EmploymentFact: # External employment, retirement, business, plan, or institution fact.
  data identifier content Entity # Entity identifying this event or classified organization, institution, or plan.
  data kind content EmploymentFactKind # Fact classification selected from EmploymentFactKind.
  data worker content Entity # Employee performing service, or the actor associated with retirement or a plan (for example, the employer establishing it); id 0 means absent.
  data employer content Entity # Employer receiving the service; for other kinds, the entity affected by the fact; id 0 means absent.
  data start content date # Start date; used only when start_present is true.
  data end content date # End date; used only when end_present is true.
  data start_present content boolean # True when a start date is recorded; false makes start irrelevant.
  data end_present content boolean # True when an end date is recorded; false makes end irrelevant.
  data purpose_1 content FactValue # Work performed (e.g. AgriculturalLabor or DomesticService), or benefits promised by a Plan (e.g. SicknessProvision); entry 1. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data purpose_2 content FactValue # Work performed (e.g. AgriculturalLabor or DomesticService), or benefits promised by a Plan (e.g. SicknessProvision); entry 2. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data location_1 content FactValue # Place where the work occurs, such as PrivateHome, UnitedStates, or a Named institution; entry 1. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data location_2 content FactValue # Place where the work occurs, such as PrivateHome, UnitedStates, or a Named institution; entry 2. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data location_3 content FactValue # Place where the work occurs, such as PrivateHome, UnitedStates, or a Named institution; entry 3. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data location_4 content FactValue # Place where the work occurs, such as PrivateHome, UnitedStates, or a Named institution; entry 4. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data reason content FactValue # Cause of retirement or termination, such as disability or a reference to a death event. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data beneficiary content Entity # Person receiving the benefit of a payment or plan; id 0 means absent.
  data multiplicity content integer # Number of represented grounded solutions or interchangeable workers; compressed worker groups require per-worker caps before scaling and must not be counted twice through matching service/payment rows.

declaration structure StatusFact: # External personal-status, enrollment, or agreement fact.
  data identifier content Entity # Entity identifying this event or classified organization, institution, or plan.
  data kind content StatusFactKind # Fact classification selected from StatusFactKind.
  data subject content Entity # Person or organization holding the status or initiating the event; id 0 means absent.
  data object content Entity # Entity affected by the event, such as the employment being terminated or the institution attended; id 0 means absent.
  data start content date # Start date; used only when start_present is true.
  data end content date # End date; used only when end_present is true.
  data start_present content boolean # True when a start date is recorded; false makes start irrelevant.
  data end_present content boolean # True when an end date is recorded; false makes end irrelevant.
  data location content FactValue # Place or institution associated with the status, such as a school or hospital. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data reason content FactValue # Cause of retirement or termination, such as disability or a reference to a death event. Absent when Known contains OtherKnownValue or Named contains an Entity with id 0.
  data multiplicity content integer # Number of represented grounded solutions or interchangeable workers; compressed worker groups require per-worker caps before scaling and must not be counted twice through matching service/payment rows.

declaration structure World: # List-based factual input; empty lists represent absent fact families. No fixed slot count or padding is required.
  data dependency_candidates content list of Entity # Dependency candidate entities; [] when none are recorded.
  data financial_facts content list of FinancialFact # Income, payment, and deduction facts; [] when none are recorded.
  data relationship_facts content list of RelationshipFact # Family, residence, life-event, and joint-return facts; [] when none are recorded.
  data employment_facts content list of EmploymentFact # Service, plan, retirement, and institution facts; [] when none are recorded.
  data status_facts content list of StatusFact # Personal status, enrollment, and agreement facts; [] when none are recorded.

declaration structure TaxPeriod: # Tax year and its calendar boundaries.
  data tax_year content integer # Calendar year used by the tax provisions.
  data first_day content date # First day of the tax period.
  data last_day content date # Last day of the tax period.

declaration structure Relationship: # Directed family relationship extracted from event agents and patients.
  data subject content Entity # Agent of the family event, whose relationship to relative is described.
  data relative content Entity # Patient of the family event, related to subject.
  data starts content list of date # Recorded start dates of the family relationship.
  data ends content list of date # Recorded end dates of the family relationship.

declaration structure MaritalResult: # Marital-status result and the spouses identified by the evaluator.
  data married content boolean # Whether the marital-status evaluator regards the taxpayer as married.
  data spouses content list of Entity # Spouse entities identified by the marital-status evaluator.

declaration same_entity content boolean
  depends on left content Entity,
             right content Entity

declaration has_agent content boolean
  depends on event content Event,
             person content Entity

declaration has_patient content boolean
  depends on event content Event,
             person content Entity

declaration overlaps_period content boolean
  depends on starts content list of date,
             ends content list of date,
             period content TaxPeriod

declaration covers_period content boolean
  depends on starts content list of date,
             ends content list of date,
             period content TaxPeriod

declaration financial_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind

declaration relationship_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind

declaration employment_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind

declaration status_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind

declaration gross_income_individual content money # One person only: sums that person's Income amounts and received Payment amounts, weighted by multiplicity; does not add a spouse's income for a joint return.
  depends on world content World,
             person content Entity,
             period content TaxPeriod

declaration has_full_year_joint_return content boolean # Tests the two filers and exact full-year return boundaries; does not combine their income or compute a filing-status conclusion.
  depends on world content World,
             taxpayer content Entity,
             spouse content Entity,
             period content TaxPeriod

declaration all_entities content list of Entity
  depends on world content World

declaration has_value content boolean
  depends on values content list of FactValue,
             expected content KnownValue

declaration dependency_candidates content list of Entity
  depends on world content World

declaration financial_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content FinancialFactKind

declaration relationship_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content RelationshipFactKind

declaration employment_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content EmploymentFactKind

declaration status_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content StatusFactKind

declaration usable_values content list of FactValue
  depends on values content list of FactValue

declaration financial_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content FinancialFact

declaration relationship_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content RelationshipFact

declaration employment_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content EmploymentFact

declaration status_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content StatusFact

declaration financial_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World

declaration relationship_and_return_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World

declaration employment_and_institution_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World

declaration personal_status_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World

declaration weighted_amounts content list of money # Scales each raw amount by event multiplicity; does not apply per-worker caps or combine separate service/payment group counts.
  depends on event content Event

## Public inputs are lists; use the normalized views below for aliases. Legacy
## numbered-slot fixtures are converted by the Python adapter before evaluation.
declaration unique_events content list of Event
  depends on rows content list of Event

declaration unique_transactions content list of Event
  depends on rows content list of Event

declaration parent_links content list of Relationship
  depends on world content World

declaration sibling_links content list of Relationship
  depends on world content World

declaration date_of_birth content optional of date
  depends on world content World,
             person content Entity,
             allow_relationship_fallback content boolean

declaration has_classification content boolean
  depends on event content Event,
             classification content KnownValue

declaration has_itemization_evidence content boolean
  depends on world content World,
             taxpayer content Entity,
             period content TaxPeriod

declaration all_input_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World

```

```catala
declaration financial_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content FinancialFactKind
  equals match kind with pattern
    -- FinancialFactKind.NoFinancialFact: EventKind.Income
    -- FinancialFactKind.Income: EventKind.Income
    -- FinancialFactKind.Payment: EventKind.Payment
    -- FinancialFactKind.Deduction: EventKind.Deduction

declaration relationship_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content RelationshipFactKind
  equals match kind with pattern
    -- RelationshipFactKind.NoRelationshipFact: EventKind.Marriage
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Marriage: EventKind.Marriage
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Birth: EventKind.Birth
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Death: EventKind.Death
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Residence: EventKind.Residence
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Migration: EventKind.Migration
    -- RelationshipFactKind.LegalSeparation: EventKind.LegalSeparation
    -- RelationshipFactKind.JointReturn: EventKind.JointReturn
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Son: EventKind.Son
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Daughter: EventKind.Daughter
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Father: EventKind.Father
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Mother: EventKind.Mother
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Brother: EventKind.Brother
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Sister: EventKind.Sister
    -- RelationshipFactKind.Sibling: EventKind.Sibling

declaration employment_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content EmploymentFactKind
  equals match kind with pattern
    -- EmploymentFactKind.NoEmploymentFact: EventKind.Service
    -- EmploymentFactKind.Service: EventKind.Service
    -- EmploymentFactKind.Retirement: EventKind.Retirement
    -- EmploymentFactKind.Business: EventKind.Business
    -- EmploymentFactKind.BusinessTrust: EventKind.BusinessTrust
    -- EmploymentFactKind.Plan: EventKind.Plan
    -- EmploymentFactKind.Hospital: EventKind.Hospital
    -- EmploymentFactKind.MedicalInstitution: EventKind.MedicalInstitution
    -- EmploymentFactKind.PenalInstitution: EventKind.PenalInstitution
    -- EmploymentFactKind.EducationalInstitution: EventKind.EducationalInstitution
    -- EmploymentFactKind.NursesTrainingSchool: EventKind.NursesTrainingSchool
    -- EmploymentFactKind.InternationalOrganization: EventKind.InternationalOrganization
    -- EmploymentFactKind.AmericanEmployer: EventKind.AmericanEmployer

declaration status_event_kind content EventKind
  depends on kind content StatusFactKind
  equals match kind with pattern
    -- StatusFactKind.NoStatusFact: EventKind.Enrollment
    -- StatusFactKind.Enrollment: EventKind.Enrollment
    -- StatusFactKind.Termination: EventKind.Termination
    -- StatusFactKind.Incarceration: EventKind.Incarceration
    -- StatusFactKind.ItemizeDeductions: EventKind.ItemizeDeductions
    -- StatusFactKind.Blindness: EventKind.Blindness
    -- StatusFactKind.Disability: EventKind.Disability
    -- StatusFactKind.AttendingClasses: EventKind.AttendingClasses
    -- StatusFactKind.MedicalPatient: EventKind.MedicalPatient
    -- StatusFactKind.NonresidentAlien: EventKind.NonresidentAlien
    -- StatusFactKind.Citizenship: EventKind.Citizenship
    -- StatusFactKind.UnemploymentCompensationAgreement:
        EventKind.UnemploymentCompensationAgreement

declaration usable_values content list of FactValue
  depends on values content list of FactValue
  equals list of value among values such that
    match value with pattern
    -- FactValue.Known content known: known != KnownValue.OtherKnownValue
    -- FactValue.Named content named: named.id != 0

declaration financial_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content FinancialFact
  equals
    if value.kind = FinancialFactKind.NoFinancialFact then [] else
        [Event {
          -- identifier: value.identifier
          -- kind: financial_event_kind of value.kind
          -- agents: list of person among [value.agent]
                     such that person.id != 0
          -- patients: list of person among [value.patient]
                       such that person.id != 0
          -- starts: if value.start_present then [value.start] else []
          -- ends: if value.end_present then [value.end] else []
          -- amounts: [value.amount]
          -- purposes: usable_values of [value.purpose_1; value.purpose_2]
          -- locations: []
          -- means: usable_values of [value.means]
          -- reasons: []
          -- beneficiaries: list of person among [value.beneficiary]
                            such that person.id != 0
          -- countries: [] -- types: [] -- destinations: []
          -- multiplicity: value.multiplicity }]

declaration relationship_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content RelationshipFact
  equals
    if value.kind = RelationshipFactKind.NoRelationshipFact then [] else
        [Event {
          -- identifier: value.identifier
          -- kind: relationship_event_kind of value.kind
          -- agents: list of person among
                       [value.subject_1; value.subject_2;
                        value.subject_3; value.subject_4]
                     such that person.id != 0
          -- patients: list of person among
                         [value.relative_1; value.relative_2]
                       such that person.id != 0
          -- starts: if value.start_present then [value.start] else []
          -- ends: if value.end_present then [value.end] else []
          -- amounts: [] -- purposes: [] -- locations: [] -- means: []
          -- reasons: [] -- beneficiaries: [] -- countries: [] -- types: []
          -- destinations: [] -- multiplicity: value.multiplicity }]

declaration employment_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content EmploymentFact
  equals
    if value.kind = EmploymentFactKind.NoEmploymentFact then [] else
        [Event {
          -- identifier: value.identifier
          -- kind: employment_event_kind of value.kind
          -- agents: list of person among [value.worker]
                     such that person.id != 0
          -- patients: list of person among [value.employer]
                       such that person.id != 0
          -- starts: if value.start_present then [value.start] else []
          -- ends: if value.end_present then [value.end] else []
          -- amounts: []
          -- purposes: usable_values of [value.purpose_1; value.purpose_2]
          -- locations: usable_values of
                          [value.location_1; value.location_2;
                           value.location_3; value.location_4]
          -- means: [] -- reasons: usable_values of [value.reason]
          -- beneficiaries: list of person among [value.beneficiary]
                            such that person.id != 0
          -- countries: [] -- types: [] -- destinations: []
          -- multiplicity: value.multiplicity }]

declaration status_fact_values content list of Event
  depends on value content StatusFact
  equals
    if value.kind = StatusFactKind.NoStatusFact then [] else
        [Event {
          -- identifier: value.identifier
          -- kind: status_event_kind of value.kind
          -- agents: list of person among [value.subject]
                     such that person.id != 0
          -- patients: list of person among [value.object]
                       such that person.id != 0
          -- starts: if value.start_present then [value.start] else []
          -- ends: if value.end_present then [value.end] else []
          -- amounts: [] -- purposes: []
          -- locations: usable_values of [value.location]
          -- means: [] -- reasons: usable_values of [value.reason]
          -- beneficiaries: [] -- countries: [] -- types: []
          -- destinations: [] -- multiplicity: value.multiplicity }]

declaration financial_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World
  equals
    unique_events of
      (combine all fact among world.financial_facts in events initially []
       with events ++ (financial_fact_values of fact))

declaration relationship_and_return_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World
  equals
    unique_events of
      (combine all fact among world.relationship_facts in events initially []
       with events ++ (relationship_fact_values of fact))

declaration employment_and_institution_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World
  equals
    unique_events of
      (combine all fact among world.employment_facts in events initially []
       with events ++ (employment_fact_values of fact))

declaration personal_status_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World
  equals
    unique_events of
      (combine all fact among world.status_facts in events initially []
       with events ++ (status_fact_values of fact))

declaration weighted_amounts content list of money # Scales each raw amount by event multiplicity; does not apply per-worker caps or combine separate service/payment group counts.
  depends on event content Event
  equals map each amount among event.amounts to
    amount * (decimal of event.multiplicity)

declaration same_entity content boolean
  depends on left content Entity,
             right content Entity
  equals left.id != 0 and right.id != 0
         and left.id = right.id and left.kind = right.kind

declaration has_agent content boolean
  depends on event content Event,
             person content Entity
  equals exists candidate among event.agents
         such that same_entity of candidate, person

declaration has_patient content boolean
  depends on event content Event,
             person content Entity
  equals exists candidate among event.patients
         such that same_entity of candidate, person

declaration overlaps_period content boolean
  depends on starts content list of date,
             ends content list of date,
             period content TaxPeriod
  equals
    (starts = [] or exists start among starts such that start <= period.last_day)
    and (ends = [] or exists ending among ends such that period.first_day <= ending)

declaration covers_period content boolean
  depends on starts content list of date,
             ends content list of date,
             period content TaxPeriod
  equals
    (exists start among starts such that start = period.first_day)
    and (exists ending among ends such that ending = period.last_day)

declaration financial_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind
  equals list of event among (financial_events of world) such that event.kind = kind

declaration relationship_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind
  equals list of event among (relationship_and_return_events of world)
         such that event.kind = kind

declaration employment_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind
  equals list of event among (employment_and_institution_events of world)
         such that event.kind = kind

declaration status_events_of_kind content list of Event
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind
  equals list of event among (personal_status_events of world)
         such that event.kind = kind

declaration relationship_events content list of Relationship
  depends on world content World,
             kind content EventKind
  equals
    combine all rows
      among
        (map each event among (relationship_events_of_kind of world, kind) to
          combine all child
            among event.agents
            in pairs initially []
            with pairs ++
              (map each parent among event.patients to
                Relationship {
                  -- subject: child
                  -- relative: parent
                  -- starts: event.starts
                  -- ends: event.ends }))
      in result initially []
      with result ++ rows

declaration gross_income_individual content money # One person only: sums that person's Income amounts and received Payment amounts, weighted by multiplicity; does not add a spouse's income for a joint return.
  depends on world content World,
             person content Entity,
             period content TaxPeriod
  equals
    Money.sum of
      (combine all event among
        (unique_transactions of
          (list of receipt among (financial_events of world) such that
            ((receipt.kind = EventKind.Income and has_agent of receipt, person)
             or (receipt.kind = EventKind.Payment and has_patient of receipt, person))
            and overlaps_period of receipt.starts, receipt.ends, period))
       in amounts initially [] with amounts ++ (weighted_amounts of event))

declaration has_full_year_joint_return content boolean # Tests the two filers and exact full-year return boundaries; does not combine their income or compute a filing-status conclusion.
  depends on world content World,
             taxpayer content Entity,
             spouse content Entity,
             period content TaxPeriod
  equals exists event among
           (relationship_events_of_kind of world, EventKind.JointReturn)
         such that has_agent of event, taxpayer
                   and has_agent of event, spouse
                   and covers_period of event.starts, event.ends, period

declaration all_entities content list of Entity
  depends on world content World
  equals
    dependency_candidates of world

declaration has_value content boolean
  depends on values content list of FactValue,
             expected content KnownValue
  equals exists value among values such that
    match value with pattern
    -- FactValue.Known content known: known = expected
    -- FactValue.Named content name: false

declaration dependency_candidates content list of Entity
  depends on world content World
  equals
    list of candidate among world.dependency_candidates
    such that candidate.id != 0

```

```catala

declaration all_input_events content list of Event
  depends on world content World
  equals
    (combine all fact among world.financial_facts in events initially []
        with events ++ (financial_fact_values of fact))
    ++ (combine all fact among world.relationship_facts in events initially []
        with events ++ (relationship_fact_values of fact))
    ++ (combine all fact among world.employment_facts in events initially []
        with events ++ (employment_fact_values of fact))
    ++ (combine all fact among world.status_facts in events initially []
        with events ++ (status_fact_values of fact))

declaration unique_events content list of Event
  depends on rows content list of Event
  equals combine all candidate among rows in kept initially []
    with if exists previous among kept such that
      same_entity of candidate.identifier, previous.identifier
        and candidate.kind = previous.kind
    then kept else kept ++ [candidate]

declaration unique_transactions content list of Event
  depends on rows content list of Event
  equals combine all candidate among rows in kept initially []
    with if exists previous among kept such that
      same_entity of candidate.identifier, previous.identifier
    then kept else kept ++ [candidate]

declaration parent_links content list of Relationship
  depends on world content World
  equals
    let children equals (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Son)
      ++ (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Daughter) in
    let parents equals (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Father)
      ++ (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Mother) in
    let oriented equals children ++ (map each parent among parents to
      Relationship { -- subject: parent.relative -- relative: parent.subject
        -- starts: parent.starts -- ends: parent.ends }) in
    combine all candidate among oriented in kept initially []
      with if exists previous among kept such that
        same_entity of candidate.subject, previous.subject
          and same_entity of candidate.relative, previous.relative
          and candidate.starts = previous.starts and candidate.ends = previous.ends
      then kept else kept ++ [candidate]

declaration sibling_links content list of Relationship
  depends on world content World
  equals
    let rows equals (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Brother)
      ++ (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Sister)
      ++ (relationship_events of world, EventKind.Sibling) in
    combine all candidate among rows in kept initially []
      with if exists previous among kept such that
        ((same_entity of candidate.subject, previous.subject
          and same_entity of candidate.relative, previous.relative)
         or (same_entity of candidate.subject, previous.relative
          and same_entity of candidate.relative, previous.subject))
        and candidate.starts = previous.starts and candidate.ends = previous.ends
      then kept else kept ++ [candidate]

declaration date_of_birth content optional of date
  depends on world content World,
             person content Entity,
             allow_relationship_fallback content boolean
  equals
    let explicit_dates equals
      combine all event among (relationship_events_of_kind of world, EventKind.Birth)
      in dates initially [] with if has_agent of event, person
        then dates ++ event.starts else dates in
    match (List.first_element of explicit_dates) with pattern
    -- Present content born: Present content born
    -- Absent:
      if not allow_relationship_fallback then Absent else
        let candidates equals combine all event
          among (relationship_and_return_events of world)
          in dates initially [] with if
            (event.kind = EventKind.Son or event.kind = EventKind.Daughter)
              and has_agent of event, person
            then dates ++ event.starts else dates in
        List.first_element of
          (combine all candidate among candidates in earliest initially []
           with match (List.first_element of earliest) with pattern
           -- Absent: [candidate]
           -- Present content previous:
             if candidate < previous then [candidate] else earliest)

declaration has_classification content boolean
  depends on event content Event,
             classification content KnownValue
  equals has_value of event.purposes, classification
    or has_value of event.locations, classification

declaration has_itemization_evidence content boolean
  depends on world content World,
             taxpayer content Entity,
             period content TaxPeriod
  equals
    (exists election among (status_events_of_kind of world, EventKind.ItemizeDeductions)
     such that has_agent of election, taxpayer
       and overlaps_period of election.starts, election.ends, period)
    or (exists deduction among (financial_events_of_kind of world, EventKind.Deduction)
      such that has_agent of deduction, taxpayer
        and exists start among deduction.starts such that
          period.first_day <= start and start <= period.last_day)

```
